  "description": "The client for Shiny.Net.HttpServer.FileSync: keeps a local folder and the server in sync both ways, Dropbox-style. Changed files are split into content-defined chunks and only the chunks the other side lacks are moved; chunks already on the device (from the old version of a file or any other file) are reused, never downloaded again. Transfers run through Shiny.Net.Http, so they continue in the background on iOS and Android and resume after a dropped connection. Conflicts become conflicted copies, not lost edits.",
